    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm looking into some options for moving our secondary production lines out of East Asia to diversify our supply chain. We're looking at a few regions: Eastern Europe, Southeast Asia, and parts of Sub-Saharan Africa. Can you give me a breakdown of the labor force characteristics in these areas? Specifically, I need to know about the general work ethic, how reliable the workers are for high-precision tasks, and what the local management capabilities look like for overseeing large teams. Need to weigh the risks before we commit.",
