      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Labor characteristics vary significantly across these regions, requiring careful due diligence. Generally, Eastern Europe offers a workforce with established manufacturing experience and high proficiency in precision tasks. Southeast Asia presents a large, adaptable labor pool often suited for high-volume production, while Sub-Saharan Africa offers lower operational costs paired with a developing, versatile workforce. Regarding management, established business practices are strongest in Eastern Europe, requiring careful vetting for local leadership capabilities in the other two areas.",
